Reclaim anonymous volumes when deleting pods

Remove anonymous volumes with their containers so devcontainer mounts
and image-defined volumes do not accumulate after deletion or
recreation. Keep named volumes available for users who opt into
persistent storage.

Declare the development image's nested Docker and Podman stores with
VOLUME so each container owns its storage and deletion can reclaim it.
Leave image-volume handling on Kubernetes to the container runtime.

Cover cleanup of both anonymous volume sources and preservation of an
implicitly created named volume that overrides an image volume.
